In `checkIfIsAvailable` (packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/slots.ts), the working-hours check computes both `start` and `end` from `slotStartTime`:
```ts
const start = slotStartTime.hour() * 60 + slotStartTime.minute();
const end = slotStartTime.hour() * 60 + slotStartTime.minute();
```
So `end` never reflects the slot’s actual end (it should be derived from `slotEndTime`). As a result, a slot that starts within working hours but extends past `workingHour.endTime` will not be rejected, matching the finding’s example. This logic is in the “no date override exists” path, so it affects normal days as described.

